# HOWTO — REQ-001 Local Execution

## Prerequisites

- Python 3.12+
- Docker (for integration tests)
- pip

## 1. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r runs/kit/REQ-001/ci/requirements.txt
```

## 2. Run unit tests (no infrastructure required)

```bash
PYTHONPATH=runs/kit/REQ-001/src \
  python -m pytest runs/kit/REQ-001/test/ \
    -m "not integration" \
    -v --tb=short \
    --cov=runs/kit/REQ-001/src/shared \
    --cov-report=term-missing \
    --cov-fail-under=80
```

Expected: all unit tests pass, coverage ≥ 80%.

## 3. Start LocalStack (for AWS integration tests)

```bash
docker run -d --name localstack \
  -p 4566:4566 \
  -e SERVICES=s3,sqs,sns,secretsmanager,logs \
  -e DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1 \
  localstack/localstack:latest
```

Wait ~10 seconds for startup, then:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=runs/kit/REQ-001/src \
DEPLOYMENT_PROFILE=aws \
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4566 \
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=test \
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=test \
  python -m pytest runs/kit/REQ-001/test/ \
    -m integration -k "Aws" \
    -v --tb=short
```

Expected: AWS integration tests pass (put/get/delete object).

## 4. Start MinIO (for on-prem integration tests)

```bash
docker run -d --name minio \
  -p 9000:9000 -p 9001:9001 \
  -e MINIO_ROOT_USER=minioadmin \
  -e MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=minioadmin \
  minio/minio:latest server /data --console-address ":9001"
```

Wait ~5 seconds for startup, then:

```bash
